WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.000
With a famously conservative lead actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.980
Sound of Freedom was already on the path to&nbsp;
controversy. Add a dash of QAnon affiliation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:12.660
and it's no surprise that the 2023 action&nbsp;
flick is raising eyebrows across the globe.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:18.240
Sound of Freedom is one of 2023's most&nbsp;
unexpected success stories. Within two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.600
weeks of its July 4th release, the&nbsp;
independent action-thriller grossed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.880
over $85 million at the box office and brought&nbsp;
Jim Caviezel back into the Hollywood spotlight.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.880
The former The Passion of the&nbsp;
Christ star plays Tim Ballard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:35.160
a former government agent who goes rogue to take&nbsp;
down a child trafficking ring. While Caviezel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.660
himself has become known for his inflammatory&nbsp;
politics, his character draws inspiration from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:44.460
a real-life figure who's dedicated his career to&nbsp;
a very particular and controversial line of work.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:49.140
Tim Ballard is a former undercover operative&nbsp;
for the U.S. Department of Homeland Security.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.820
After leaving the government agency, he&nbsp;
founded Operation Underground Railroad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.000
a nonprofit organization that's&nbsp;
dedicated to fighting real-life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.611
human trafficking rings all around the world.

00:00:59.611 --> 00:01:04.440
Of course, Ballard's work has also made him a&nbsp;
source of controversy. He's outspoken about his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.280
politics and he's been linked to conspiracy&nbsp;
theories pertaining to the exploitation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.540
children. For this reason, Sound of Freedom&nbsp;
has attracted its fair share of critics, some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:17.665
of whom have big names. Rolling Stone succinctly&nbsp;
summarized their thoughts on the film, writing,

00:01:17.665 --> 00:01:20.820
"The QAnon-tinged thriller about&nbsp;
child-trafficking is designed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.520
appeal to the conscience of&nbsp;
a conspiracy-addled boomer."

00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:26.553
"God's children are not for sale."

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.380
There are aspects to Sound of Freedom's&nbsp;
plot that are quite representative of how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:36.360
Ballard's story is reported to have transpired.&nbsp;
As the film depicts, Ballard really did quit his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.740
job at the Department of Homeland Security in&nbsp;
order to carry out a rescue mission. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.220
it's the mission in question that starts&nbsp;
to separate the film from reality.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.840
In Sound of Freedom, Ballard quits his job&nbsp;
to rescue a young girl from the hands of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:53.340
a Colombian child trafficking organization.&nbsp;
However, while speaking to The Daily Signal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:58.380
Ballard explained that his federal superiors told&nbsp;
him to abort missions in both Haiti and Colombia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.160
which he refused to do as he felt it&nbsp;
defeated the purpose of his duties.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:06.300
Ballard described both those missions as&nbsp;
"major cases," which could have had huge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:12.000
impacts on human trafficking worldwide. When he&nbsp;
received instructions to come home, he refused.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.520
In the same interview, Ballard revealed that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.700
was able to carry out the missions&nbsp;
thanks to funding from Glenn Beck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.860
a conservative political commentator who's&nbsp;
worked for CNN, Fox News, and TheBlaze TV.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:27.480
After completing the rescues, Ballard&nbsp;
formed Operation Underground Railroad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.860
in 2013. According to the foundation's&nbsp;
website, the group works with government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.220
and law enforcement agencies, both&nbsp;
domestically and internationally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.700
to devise strategies that will assist&nbsp;
in the fight against human trafficking.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.580
These strategies include gathering intelligence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:46.080
offering resources, and providing care&nbsp;
to survivors. They've also been known to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.620
carry out sting operations and share the&nbsp;
footage of their rescues on social media.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.720
While the Operation Underground Railroad's efforts&nbsp;
seem noble in theory, they have also been the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.280
subject of some controversy. Most notably,&nbsp;
the organization has been linked with QAnon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.700
a far-right conspiracy theory movement&nbsp;
that believes Democratic politicians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:07.020
and Hollywood celebrities are involved in&nbsp;
the operation of child trafficking rings.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:11.700
Ballard and Operation Underground Railroad have&nbsp;
denied any association with the movement, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.380
their methods for researching and spreading the&nbsp;
word about human trafficking are markedly similar.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.612 --> 00:03:19.612
Discussing QAnon with The New&nbsp;
York Times, Ballard even stated,

00:03:19.612 --> 00:03:22.920
"Some of these theories have allowed&nbsp;
people to open their eyes. So now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:26.820
it's our job to flood the space with real&nbsp;
information so the facts can be shared."

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.500
These days, however, even Ballard appears to be&nbsp;
distancing himself from Operation Underground&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.240
Railroad. Vice reported that he parted ways&nbsp;
with the organization before Sound of Freedom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:40.440
was released, and he has since co-founded&nbsp;
a new endeavor known as The Spear Fund.

